# Architecture Enforcement

Guide AI to place code in the correct architectural layer (API, Service, CRUD, Models, Schemas).

<rule>
name: layered_architecture
description: Ensures code placement follows the API -> Service -> CRUD -> DB structure.
filters:
  - type: intent
    pattern: "(create|implement|add|define)_.*(endpoint|route|logic|query|database|model|schema)"
  - type: content
    # Look for database logic outside crud, business logic outside services, etc.
    pattern: "(db\\.execute|session\\.exec).*(app/api/|app/services/)|(calculate|process|complex_logic).*(app/api/|app/crud/)"

actions:
  - type: reject
    conditions:
      # Reject direct DB calls from API layer
      - pattern: "(db\\.execute|session\\.exec|select\\(|update\\(|insert\\(|delete\\().*\\n.*@router\\."
        target_path: "app/api/"
        message: "API endpoints in `app/api/` should not perform direct database operations. Call functions in the Service layer (`app/services/`) instead."
      # Reject complex business logic in API layer
      - pattern: "(if.*else|for.*in.*\\n.*calculate|process_data.*\\n.*@router\\.)" # Simplified pattern
        target_path: "app/api/"
        message: "Complex business logic should reside in the Service layer (`app/services/`), not directly in API endpoints."
      # Reject complex business logic in CRUD layer
      - pattern: "(if.*else|for.*in.*\\n.*calculate|process_data)" # Simplified pattern
        target_path: "app/crud/"
        message: "CRUD functions (`app/crud/`) should only handle direct database interactions. Place complex business logic in the Service layer (`app/services/`)."

  - type: suggest
    message: |
      Follow the project architecture:
      1. API Layer (`app/api/`): Handles HTTP requests/responses, calls Service layer. Keep thin.
      2. Service Layer (`app/services/`): Contains core business logic, calls CRUD layer.
      3. CRUD Layer (`app/crud/`): Handles direct database operations using SQLAlchemy models.
      4. Models (`app/models/`): SQLAlchemy ORM definitions.
      5. Schemas (`app/schemas/`): Pydantic API data definitions.
</rule>